  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds (p5 Total Governmental Funds); fund balances 362,250 -> 405,224; CDBG Rehab Fund transfer out 8,466 to the Sewer Fund. Beginning cash not printed (no prior-year balance sheet); ending cash = governmental funds balance sheet cash 401,738 + county treasurer cash 3,486 = total assets 405,224 (p4). Business-type from the accrual proprietary statement p7 (Total); expenses 657,782 tie to the Statement of Activities (p2); transfer in 8,466. Proprietary cash flows (p8-9) left null as in later years. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position, component unit excluded. Detail: General Fund from the departmental combining statement (p13-14), which supersedes the General Fund budget schedule (p10); Street Fund from its budget schedule (p11); CDBG Rehab Fund budget schedule (p12) has only the transfer out (revenue and spending actuals nil). No enterprise budget schedules. 'Charges, admission, and rental fees' 12,113 split by the departmental/Street schedules. Read pages 1-14 of 14"
